<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Franz Joseph Spiegler</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1691–1757</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franz-joseph-i">Franz Joseph</a> Spiegler was a German painter of the late baroque, active mainly in upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabia">Swabia</a> and around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-constance">Lake Constance</a>. His largest work is the cycle of ceiling frescoes in the abbey church of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwiefalten">Zwiefalten</a>, painted from 1751, whose nave fresco is one of the largest of the period. He also painted altarpieces and church frescoes across the region and died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstanz">Konstanz</a> in 1757.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/franz-joseph-spiegler.jpg" alt="Franz Joseph Spiegler" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franz Joseph Spiegler · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zwiefalten_Muenster_Deckengemaelde.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
